{
 "meta": {
  "name": "units_pi",
  "note": "Hand-written. pi's reference digits and the cases that check the Calculator's enclosure of pi (Principia.Exact.piInterval, piPowBounds), the sign of a polynomial at a power of pi (polySignAtPiPow), and the strike-rule wrappers across powers of pi. The correctness of the enclosure rests on these vectors, not on a proof (decision D1 leaves Mathlib's real numbers out).",
  "reference": {
   "digits": "3.",
   "decimals": 1399,
   "source": "Computed, not copied: mpmath 1.4.1 (PyPI) and pidigits 0.5 (PyPI; Gibbons' unbounded spigot with Gosper's series), which agree on every digit. The published tables (OEIS A000796's b-file, Project Gutenberg eBook 50) were not reachable from the session that wrote this file; an Operator can compare these digits with either.",
   "meaning": "pi lies in [digits, digits + 10^-decimals)",
   "sha256": "7b2837ba174a1b91450613114da37700959badda709ef4507eb7a437cbf99000",
   "sha256_of": "the 1400 digits as ASCII, without the point or any newline, from 3141 to the last",
   "tools": "mpmath and pidigits made these vectors; nothing in the build or the checks installs them"
  }
 },
